{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 7,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.1,
            0.104,
            0.138,
            0.119
          ],
          "content": "120"
        },
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.782,
            0.104,
            0.899,
            0.12
          ],
          "content": "MATHEMATICS"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.15,
            0.624,
            0.188
          ],
          "content": "**Example 4 :** In a right triangle ABC, right-angled at B, if tan A = 1, then verify that"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.195,
            0.285,
            0.212
          ],
          "content": "2 sin A cos A = 1."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.225,
            0.632,
            0.268
          ],
          "content": "**Solution :** In   ABC, tan $\\mathrm { A }   =   { \\frac { \\mathrm { B C } } { \\mathrm { A B } } } = 1$ (see Fig 8.11)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.286,
            0.139,
            0.303
          ],
          "content": "i.e.,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.43,
            0.284,
            0.535,
            0.303
          ],
          "content": "\\mathrm { B C } = \\mathrm { A B }",
          "image_source": "images/page_7_equation_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.655,
            0.148,
            0.872,
            0.289
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.718,
                0.299,
                0.813,
                0.318
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 8.11"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_7_image_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.317,
            0.564,
            0.336
          ],
          "content": "Let $\\mathrm{AB} = \\mathrm{BC} = k$ , where k is a positive number."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.361,
            0.156,
            0.378
          ],
          "content": "Now,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.428,
            0.355,
            0.702,
            0.433
          ],
          "content": "\\begin{aligned} AC  &= \\sqrt{ AB ^2 +  BC ^2} \\\\&= \\sqrt{\\left(k\\right)^2 + \\left(k\\right)^2} = k\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}",
          "image_source": "images/page_7_equation_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.471,
            0.205,
            0.49
          ],
          "content": "Therefore,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.411,
            0.456,
            0.868,
            0.499
          ],
          "content": "$\\sin A = \\frac{BC}{AC} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$ and cos $\\mathrm{A} = \\frac{\\mathrm{AB}}{\\mathrm{AC}} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.515,
            0.851,
            0.564
          ],
          "content": "So, 2 sin A cos $2\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)\\left(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\right)=1,$ which is the required value."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.575,
            0.595,
            0.639
          ],
          "content": "**Example 5 :** In $\\mathrm { { \\it { K } } } \\mathrm { { \\it { O P Q } } }$ , right-angled at P, $\\mathrm { O P } = 7$ cm and $\\mathrm{OQ} \\sim \\mathrm{PQ} = 1$ cm (see Fig. 8.12). Determine the values of sin Q and cos Q."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.651,
            0.403,
            0.67
          ],
          "content": "**Solution :** In $\\Delta \\; \\mathrm { O P Q } ,$ , we have"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.309,
            0.682,
            0.502,
            0.704
          ],
          "content": "\\mathrm{OQ^{2}} = \\mathrm{OP^{2}} + \\mathrm{PQ^{2}}",
          "image_source": "images/page_7_equation_17.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.717,
            0.139,
            0.736
          ],
          "content": "i.e.,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.26,
            0.715,
            0.611,
            0.737
          ],
          "content": "(1 + \\mathrm{PQ})^2 = \\mathrm{OP}^2 + \\mathrm{PQ}^2 \\quad (\\mathrm{Why?})",
          "image_source": "images/page_7_equation_19.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.75,
            0.139,
            0.768
          ],
          "content": "i.e.,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.212,
            0.748,
            0.502,
            0.769
          ],
          "content": "1 + \\mathrm{PQ}^{2} + 2\\mathrm{PQ} = \\mathrm{OP}^{2} + \\mathrm{PQ}^{2}",
          "image_source": "images/page_7_equation_21.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.783,
            0.138,
            0.802
          ],
          "content": "i.e.,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.278,
            0.782,
            0.416,
            0.802
          ],
          "content": "1 + 2\\mathrm{PQ} = 7^{2}",
          "image_source": "images/page_7_equation_23.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.532,
            0.783,
            0.61,
            0.803
          ],
          "content": "(Why?)"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.741,
            0.583,
            0.873,
            0.824
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_7_image_25.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.814,
            0.714,
            0.835
          ],
          "content": "i.e., PQ = 24 cm and OQ = 1 + PQ = 25 cm"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.852,
            0.597,
            0.896
          ],
          "content": "So, $\\sin Q = { \\frac { 7 } { 2 5 } }$ and cos $\\mathsf { Q } = { \\frac { 2 4 } { 2 5 } } \\cdotp$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.758,
            0.836,
            0.858,
            0.855
          ],
          "content": "Fig. 8.12"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.435,
            0.966,
            0.564,
            0.982
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        }
      ]
    }
